-- title:
--   Generic fibre of the Igusa scheme is the curve model
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$, and write $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $\bar\jmath =$ `jBar N` be the coefficientwise image of the $j$-expansion inside `modularFunctionFieldBar N` $=$ `laurentBaseChange` $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ `(modularFunctionFieldFull N)`. Assume $\bar\jmath$ is transcendental over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and nonzero, and that `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is finite-dimensional over each of $\bar{\mathbb Q}(\bar\jmath)$ and $\bar{\mathbb Q}(\bar\jmath^{-1})$. Assume further given $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-algebra isomorphisms $e_{\mathrm{fin}} : \bar{\mathbb Q} \otimes_{\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}} A_{\mathrm{fin}} \to R_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $e_{\infty} : \bar{\mathbb Q} \otimes_{\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}} A_{\infty} \to R_{\infty}$, where $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ`, $A_{\infty} =$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ` are the two Igusa chart algebras over $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}$ and $R_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $R_{\infty}$ are the subalgebras of elements of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` integral over $\bar{\mathbb Q}[\bar\jmath]$, resp. $\bar{\mathbb Q}[\bar\jmath^{-1}]$, subject to the normalisations $e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b) =$ `coeffEmb` $\bar{\mathbb Q}\,(b)$ for all $b \in A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and likewise for $e_{\infty}$. Let $M_\eta =$ `CurveModel.ofGenerator` $\bar{\mathbb Q}\,\bar\jmath$ be the glued two-chart integral proper smooth relative-dimension-one model of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ attached to $\bar\jmath$. Then there is an isomorphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ to the pullback of `igusaTo N ℓ` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)} \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ such that: (i) $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection is $M_\eta$`.toBase`, so $e_\eta$ is a morphism over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; (ii) on the finite chart, `CurveModel.ι₀` followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $e_{\mathrm{fin}} \circ$ `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight` followed by `ιFin N ℓ`, and symmetrically `CurveModel.ιInf` with $e_{\infty}$ and `ιInf N ℓ`; and (iii) for every $g \in \operatorname{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ and all $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta$ (sections of $M_\eta.$`toBase`), if the first-projection composite of $x'$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by that of $x$, then $M_\eta.$`pointEquivPlace` $x' =$ `arithmeticGalois (modularFunctionFieldFull N) g` $\cdot\; M_\eta.$`pointEquivPlace` $x$, the action being that of the semilinear automorphism attached to $g$ on places.
--
--   This identifies the generic fibre of the two-chart Igusa scheme over $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}$ with the curve model of the modular function field over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ generated by $j$, pinning the isomorphism chart by chart and recording that it transports the Galois action on $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-points to the arithmetic action on places. It feeds [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_curveModel_iso_genericFibre_galoisCompat_chartPin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_curveModel_iso_genericFibre_galoisCompat_chartPin), and through it the construction of a relative model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}$ with compatible fibre identifications.
